Subject: Fuses a chained property read into one register instruction

What this does
  Fuses a chained property read into one register instruction.

Why we need it
  So each pair was paying a dispatch and an operand decode for one logical step.

What it adds
  A new `ROP_get_field_chain` performs both reads and writes both destinations; both PIC sites quicken independently through a `ROP_get_field_chain_own` spelling used only when both sites are cached own slots, so the own handler drops the kind and prototype tests; the first store is inlined because `T_SET_NEXT` would dispatch before the second read, with the rare last-reference case continuing in a separate free handler; the fusion pass fires only on IR-adjacent pairs whose second receiver is the first destination, with distinct destinations and no branch/catch/finally target or block leader between them, and runs after register allocation, the ownership analysis and dead-store elision; site allocation now assigns a dense PIC site to every `s` operand, not only the first.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.
